CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*mm->mmu_notifier_lock)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct percpu_rw_semaphore)...)
#130: FILE: include/linux/mmu_notifier.h:507:
+	mm->mmu_notifier_lock = kzalloc(sizeof(struct percpu_rw_semaphore), GFP_KERNEL);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

WARNING:IN_ATOMIC: use of in_atomic() is incorrect outside core kernel code
#149: FILE: include/linux/mmu_notifier.h:526:
+	if (!in_atomic()) {

in_atomic() is not for driver use so any such use is reported as an ERROR.
Also in_atomic() is often used to determine if sleeping is permitted,
but it is not reliable in this use model.  Therefore its use is
strongly discouraged.

However, in_atomic() is ok for core kernel use.

See: https://lore.kernel.org/lkml/20080320201723.b87b3732.akpm@linux-foundation.org/

